    "result_text": "The build passes. \n\nI implemented the change in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` \u2014 the REST endpoint handling `POST /api/owners`:\n\n- Added a `CITY_CAPACITY = 50` constant and a `countOwnersInCity(String city)` helper (case-insensitive, matching the existing `nextCustomerCode` logic, which I refactored to reuse the helper).\n- Before saving a new owner, if the owner's city already contains 50 or more owners, the create is rejected with `409 Conflict` via `ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.CONFLICT, ...)`, consistent with the existing duplicate-telephone and household conflict checks.\n\nThe full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`), including the acceptance test `coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity`, which fills a fresh city to exactly 50 owners and expects the 51st create to return 409.",
