        "findings": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is clean, additive, and idiomatic for this codebase:\n\n- **Right unit / no duplication.** `countOwnersInCity` extracts the case-insensitive per-city count that previously lived inline in `nextCustomerCode`, and `nextCustomerCode` is refactored to reuse it. The new capacity check calls the same helper, so the counting logic now has a single home instead of being copy-pasted into the new validation.\n- **Check placement.** The `>= CITY_CAPACITY` guard sits alongside the other `CONFLICT` validations in `addOwner` (telephone-in-use, household-in-use), following the same throw-`ResponseStatusException` idiom \u2014 exactly where a maintainer would look for it.\n- **Constant placement matches local convention.** This file deliberately declares constants next to the code that uses them (`EMAIL_PATTERN` by `normalizeEmail`, `ADDRESS_ABBREVIATIONS` by `normalizeAddress`) rather than hoisting them all to the top. Putting `CITY_CAPACITY` beside `countOwnersInCity` is consistent with that pattern.\n- **Helper location.** `countOwnersInCity` lives among the other private helper methods (`countNamesakes`, `isTelephoneInUse`), so the grouping stays coherent, and it's documented in the same Javadoc style as its neighbors.\n\nNothing is becoming a catch-all and no logic is misplaced."
